   "source": [
    "Here is the Python code for image processing and prediction in your Fake Currency Detection using Deep Learning project. Run these cells in Jupyter Notebook after training and saving your model.\n",
    "1. Import libraries\n",
    "import tensorflow as tfimport numpy as npimport matplotlib.pyplot as pltfrom PIL import Image\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "2. Load the trained model\n",
    "model = tf.keras.models.load_model(\"currency_model.keras\")print(\"Model loaded successfully!\")\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "Make sure currency_model.keras is in your current working folder.\n",
    "3. Image processing\n",
    "This code loads a currency image, resizes it to 224 × 224 pixels, and normalizes its pixel values.\n",
    "image_path = r\"C:\\Users\\indus\\Downloads\\currency.jpg\"image = Image.open(image_path).convert(\"RGB\")# Resize the imageimage = image.resize((224, 224))# Convert image to NumPy arrayimage_array = np.array(image)# Normalize pixel valuesimage_array = image_array / 255.0# Add batch dimensionimage_array = np.expand_dims(image_array, axis=0)print(\"Image processed successfully!\")print(\"Image shape:\", image_array.shape)\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "Change currency.jpg to the actual name and location of your image.\n",
    "4. Display the processed image\n",
    "plt.imshow(image_array[0])plt.title(\"Processed Currency Image\")plt.axis(\"off\")plt.show()\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "5. Predict whether the currency is real or fake\n",
    "This example assumes your CNN has one sigmoid output and was trained with fake = 0 and real = 1.\n",
    "prediction = model.predict(image_array)score = float(np.squeeze(prediction))if score >= 0.5:    print(\"Prediction: REAL CURRENCY\")else:    print(\"Prediction: FAKE CURRENCY\")print(\"Model score:\", round(score, 4))\n",
    "\n",
